==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{LG.}} {{term|klump}}<ref>[http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/clump%5B1%5D clump] in Merriam-Webster's dictionary</ref> (cf. German {{term|Klumpen}}). Cognates include Danish {{term|klump|lang=da}} (probably from Low German as well<ref>{{R:ODS online|klump}}</ref>). Cf. Norwegian (bokmål) {{term|klump|lang=no}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-clump.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ʌmp}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[cluster]] or [[lump]]
# A [[thick]] [[group]] or [[bunch]], especially of [[bush]]es or hair.
# A [[dull]] [[thud]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# A Clump is a mildly offensive hand gesture used to annoy and confuse the person it is aimed at. To perform a Clump, simply hold your Left hand at head height and join your thumb and finger, pointing them downwards. With your right hand, hold your left hand with your fingers and thumb pointing upwards covering the left hand and slowing pull your right hand down holding the position of your fingers and thumb pointing upwards as though you are holding an imaginary tennis ball. Do this with your right hand while keeping your left hand in the position with fingers and thumbs pointing downwards. 
# In order to make your Clump more extreme, simply reduce the speed of bringing your right hand down and pull faces at the person you aim the clump at, this is sure to annoy and confuse them. 
# Also see...Clumping (vb)

